# Workspace

Next.js App Router app in `src/`. This is **not** the Next.js from training data — read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before writing framework code, and follow deprecation notices.

## Stack

- Next.js 16 (App Router), React 19, TypeScript (strict)
- Package manager: **bun**
- Lint/format: **Biome** (`bun run lint`, `bun run format`) — do not add ESLint/Prettier
- UI: Tailwind 4, shadcn (`base-nova`), `@base-ui/react`, `lucide-react`
- Auth: **Better Auth** ([Next.js integration](https://better-auth.com/docs/integrations/next))
- Dev server: `bun run dev` on port **4555**
- Import alias: `@/*` → `./src/*`

## Conventions

- App Router only. Do not add `pages/`.
- Prefer Server Components. Add `"use client"` only for browser state, events, or Better Auth React client hooks.
- Colocate UI in `src/components`, primitives in `src/components/ui`, helpers in `src/lib`.
- Use existing shadcn primitives (`Button`, `Input`, etc.) instead of one-off styled elements.

## Better Auth

Use Better Auth for all authentication. Do not add NextAuth, Clerk, or custom session cookies.

When implementing auth, follow this layout:

- Server instance: `src/lib/auth.ts` — `getAuth()` factory (`betterAuth`, `nextCookies()` last in `plugins`). Do not export a module-level `auth` singleton; D1 is only available per request on Cloudflare.
- React client: `src/lib/auth-client.ts` (`createAuthClient` from `better-auth/react`)
- Route handler: `src/app/api/auth/[...all]/route.ts` calls `(await getAuth()).handler(request)`
- Route protection: `src/middleware.ts` (Edge). OpenNext 1.20.2 rejects Next.js 16 Node `proxy.ts`.
- Database: `getDb()` in `src/db/index.ts` — libSQL `file:local.db` during `bun run dev`, D1 binding `DB` on Cloudflare

```ts
import { getAuth } from "@/lib/auth";

export async function GET(request: Request) {
  const auth = await getAuth();
  return auth.handler(request);
}
```

- Cookie checks in `middleware.ts` are optimistic only. Always validate with `(await getAuth()).api.getSession({ headers: await headers() })` in Server Components, Server Actions, and route handlers.
- Client sign-in/up/out goes through `authClient`. Server mutations that set cookies must run where `nextCookies()` can apply.
